    "detail": "Since it's in front of the train station, the city is close, and you can walk to the night market. The bus terminal is far, but it's surprisingly close if you go through the station. The shower and toilet were clean, and the large lockers were really great. You can't eat in the booth, but you can eat while watching trains in the meeting room. Since it's a dorm, comfort can vary depending on the people in the same room, but on the first night, there was snoring, and on the second night, there was quite a bit of teeth grinding, so earplugs were necessary. Also, there's no refrigerator, so it would be nice to have one that you could use freely. They kept my stuff at the front desk when I asked, but you can't take things in and out freely...",
